00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:01.320
on just how all of us could
navigate the situation.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.810
What advice do you have for other teachers

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.790
that are feeling a little bit overwhelmed,

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:06.810
like how do you navigate this,

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:08.340
how do you keep your kids learning,

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.710
can you even try to do

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:12.310
what you would typically
do in a normal environment?

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:17.640
- I think if you focus on one platform

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.770
they already feel comfortable with,

00:14:20.770 --> 00:14:22.110
something they are familiar with.

00:14:22.110 --> 00:14:25.277
Every teacher is getting
things from their district,

00:14:25.277 --> 00:14:26.610
"Try this, try this,"

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:30.120
just as every parent is
getting a million new apps

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:33.790
that they're able to use
or a million different ways

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:37.160
to find curriculum that aligns,

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:40.540
but it's so overwhelming
for not only the teacher

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.560
who hasn't had to use
maybe the digital textbook

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.800
or hasn't had to use some
of these digital things,

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:46.800
but also the parent.

00:14:47.797 --> 00:14:50.547
